/**
 * @page cl_windows Windows
 *
 * Windows has no in-box USB/IP client. Install
 * <a href="https://github.com/vadimgrn/usbip-win2">usbip-win2</a> (Windows 10/11) or the
 * older <a href="https://github.com/cezanne/usbip-win">usbip-win</a>.
 *
 * From an **Administrator** prompt:
 *
 * @code{.bat}
 * usbip.exe attach -r 127.0.0.1 -b 1-1
 * usbip.exe port
 * usbip.exe detach -p 0
 * @endcode
 *
 * Or from usbip-win2's GUI, which lists what the server offers and attaches the bus id
 * you pick:
 *
 * @image html usbip-win2-gui.png width=700px
 *
 *
 */
